WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.134 --> 00:00:02.769 align:start size:84% position:16%
- Well, I think
something really big

00:00:02.769 --> 00:00:04.437
that's different
is Donald Trump.

00:00:04.437 --> 00:00:07.207
Because in 2016 he was
running as an outsider.

00:00:07.207 --> 00:00:10.744 align:start size:97% position:3%
He said, look, I don't have
50 years of political baggage.

00:00:10.744 --> 00:00:11.978
I'm not paying back favors.

00:00:11.978 --> 00:00:13.713
I'm an outsider,
I'm a businessman.

00:00:13.713 --> 00:00:14.914
I know how to balance a budget,

00:00:14.914 --> 00:00:16.383
I know how to cut spending

00:00:16.383 --> 00:00:19.386 align:start size:97% position:3%
and I know how to, you know,
get stuff done basically

00:00:19.386 --> 00:00:20.854
and I'll bring the troops home.

00:00:20.854 --> 00:00:24.290 align:start size:94% position:6%
And so that's why the
polls got it wrong because

00:00:24.290 --> 00:00:26.426
people voted for him
who had never voted

00:00:26.426 --> 00:00:28.128
or who hadn't voted for 20 years

00:00:28.128 --> 00:00:29.262
and so

00:00:29.262 --> 00:00:30.463
now

00:00:30.463 --> 00:00:31.698
it's four years later

00:00:31.698 --> 00:00:33.767 align:start size:84% position:16%
and we can see that
he's acted pretty much

00:00:33.767 --> 00:00:35.668 align:start size:88% position:13%
like all the
professional politicians

00:00:35.668 --> 00:00:37.537
that he's increased the deficit,

00:00:37.537 --> 00:00:39.305
he's increased the debt,

00:00:39.305 --> 00:00:41.107 align:start size:84% position:16%
still hasn't brought
the troops home.

00:00:41.107 --> 00:00:44.144 align:start size:84% position:16%
So now I think that
maybe people will say,

00:00:44.144 --> 00:00:47.213 align:start size:97% position:3%
you know, maybe republicans
are beyond hope.

00:00:47.213 --> 00:00:49.783
(upbeat music)

00:00:54.387 --> 00:00:56.056 line:0%
I'm Dave Rubin and this
is the Rubin report.

00:00:56.056 --> 00:00:59.359 line:0%
As always guys, don't forget
to subscribe to our channel

00:00:59.359 --> 00:01:01.895 line:0%
and click that pesky
notification bell.

00:01:01.895 --> 00:01:05.198 align:start size:97% position:3%
And joining me today is a
senior lecturer in psychology

00:01:05.198 --> 00:01:06.666
at Clemson university

00:01:06.666 --> 00:01:10.403 align:start size:97% position:3%
and libertarian presidential
candidate, Jo Jorgensen,

00:01:10.403 --> 00:01:12.372
welcome to the Rubin report.

00:01:12.372 --> 00:01:15.141 align:start size:94% position:6%
- Oh, so glad to be here,
thanks for having me.

00:01:15.141 --> 00:01:16.609
- Well, I'm thrilled to have you

00:01:16.609 --> 00:01:19.512 align:start position:0%
and I know for sure that my
audience is thrilled to have you

00:01:19.512 --> 00:01:23.149 align:start size:88% position:13%
because I've received
roughly 4 billion tweets

00:01:23.149 --> 00:01:25.819
saying why haven't you
had Joe Jorgensen on?

00:01:25.819 --> 00:01:27.287
So for the record,

00:01:27.287 --> 00:01:30.156 align:start size:97% position:3%
we have been trying to make
this happen for a while

00:01:30.156 --> 00:01:31.591
and we finally,

00:01:31.591 --> 00:01:33.093
we finally did make it happen.

00:01:33.093 --> 00:01:36.196
We weren't avoiding you and
you were not avoiding us.

00:01:36.196 --> 00:01:37.597
Is that fair to say?

00:01:37.597 --> 00:01:39.833 align:start size:97% position:3%
- It's just, you just
couldn't catch up to the bus,

00:01:39.833 --> 00:01:41.401
back there chasing my bus.

00:01:41.401 --> 00:01:43.470
(all laughing)

00:01:43.470 --> 00:01:44.637
- You got a powered,

00:01:44.637 --> 00:01:46.172 align:start size:88% position:13%
you got a super
powered bus over there.

00:01:46.172 --> 00:01:47.440
Okay, so there's a lot of stuff

00:01:47.440 --> 00:01:49.342
that I wanna talk to you about

00:01:49.342 --> 00:01:51.411
and I think you know a bit about

00:01:51.411 --> 00:01:53.012
my sort of political revolution

00:01:53.012 --> 00:01:56.382
and probably most of
my political stances.

00:01:56.382 --> 00:01:58.284
You may not know that
I actually did vote

00:01:58.284 --> 00:02:00.553 align:start size:97% position:3%
for the libertarian candidate
in the last election.

00:02:00.553 --> 00:02:01.955
I did vote for Gary Johnson.

00:02:01.955 --> 00:02:04.124
I had Gary Johnson on my show.

00:02:04.124 --> 00:02:06.559
I liked Gary Johnson.

00:02:06.559 --> 00:02:08.261
I don't think he was,

00:02:08.261 --> 00:02:11.064
you know, the strongest
libertarian candidate

00:02:11.064 --> 00:02:13.933
in a year that there
was a moment for it.

00:02:14.968 --> 00:02:16.736
So I guess my first question

00:02:16.736 --> 00:02:18.938
that'll probably set
up everything else is

00:02:19.939 --> 00:02:22.041
if it didn't work in 2016,

00:02:22.041 --> 00:02:25.011
when so many people
were frustrated,

00:02:25.011 --> 00:02:27.113
what is different this time?

00:02:27.113 --> 00:02:30.350 align:start size:97% position:3%
Why should the libertarians
have hoped this time?

00:02:30.350 --> 00:02:33.019 align:start size:84% position:16% line:0%
- Well, I think
something really big

00:02:33.019 --> 00:02:35.855 align:start size:94% position:6% line:0%
that's different is Donald
Trump because in 2016,

00:02:35.855 --> 00:02:37.457
he was running as an outsider.

00:02:37.457 --> 00:02:40.994
He said, "Look, I don't have
50 years of political baggage.

00:02:40.994 --> 00:02:42.228
I'm not paying back favors,

00:02:42.228 --> 00:02:43.963
I'm an outsider,
I'm a businessman,

00:02:43.963 --> 00:02:45.165
I know how to balance a budget,

00:02:45.165 --> 00:02:46.633
I know how to cut spending

00:02:46.633 --> 00:02:49.669 align:start size:97% position:3%
and I know how to, you know,
get stuff done basically

00:02:49.669 --> 00:02:51.171
and I'll bring the troops home."

00:02:51.171 --> 00:02:54.574 align:start size:94% position:6%
And so that's why the
polls got it wrong because

00:02:54.574 --> 00:02:56.709
people voted for him
who had never voted

00:02:56.709 --> 00:02:58.378 align:start size:84% position:16%
or who hadn't
voted for 20 years.

00:02:58.378 --> 00:03:02.615
And so now it's four years
later and we can see that

00:03:02.615 --> 00:03:05.785
he's acted pretty much like all
the professional politicians

00:03:05.785 --> 00:03:07.620
that he's increased the deficit,

00:03:07.620 --> 00:03:09.455
he's increased the debt,

00:03:09.455 --> 00:03:11.191 align:start size:84% position:16%
still hasn't brought
the troops home.

00:03:11.191 --> 00:03:14.260 align:start size:84% position:16%
So now I think that
maybe people will say,

00:03:14.260 --> 00:03:17.297 align:start size:94% position:6%
you know maybe republicans
are beyond hope.

00:03:17.297 --> 00:03:19.032
Now libertarians have known that

00:03:19.032 --> 00:03:21.734 align:start size:84% position:16%
republicans are
beyond hope since 1971

00:03:21.734 --> 00:03:23.303
and that's why the
party was formed

00:03:23.303 --> 00:03:26.606
after Richard Nixon stopped
acting like a Republican

00:03:26.606 --> 00:03:28.608
but maybe now the
Republican voters

00:03:28.608 --> 00:03:31.077
and let me say, there are
many fine Republican voters

00:03:31.077 --> 00:03:32.612
who want smaller government.

00:03:32.612 --> 00:03:35.815
It's Republican politicians
who aren't giving it to them.

00:03:35.815 --> 00:03:38.885 align:start size:94% position:6%
And so maybe after having
an outsider come in

00:03:38.885 --> 00:03:41.688 align:start size:97% position:3%
a businessman who supposedly
can balance a budget

00:03:41.688 --> 00:03:43.056
maybe they'll say, you know,

00:03:43.056 --> 00:03:45.124
it's time for a real outsider.

00:03:46.259 --> 00:03:48.561
- So what would you say
to the conservatives

00:03:48.561 --> 00:03:51.064
or the republicans who
want smaller government,

00:03:51.064 --> 00:03:52.365
they want lower taxes

00:03:52.365 --> 00:03:53.433
and they're looking
and they're going,

00:03:53.433 --> 00:03:55.602
okay, Trump did cut some taxes.

00:03:55.602 --> 00:03:57.136
He got rid of some regulation.

00:03:57.136 --> 00:03:59.539 align:start size:97% position:3%
We're clearly not going into
other wars at the moment.

00:03:59.539 --> 00:04:01.040
We're bringing troops home,

00:04:01.040 --> 00:04:03.076
that are basically looking
at that stuff and going,

00:04:03.076 --> 00:04:07.146 align:start size:97% position:3%
Hey, Trump did give us a bunch
of the stuff that we want.

00:04:07.146 --> 00:04:08.414
Yes, is the budget going up?

00:04:08.414 --> 00:04:10.883
Yeah, but the budgets or
is the deficit going up?

00:04:10.883 --> 00:04:12.785 align:start size:84% position:16%
Yeah, but it always
seems to go up.

00:04:12.785 --> 00:04:14.654
Do you think he's
done anything right

00:04:14.654 --> 00:04:16.956
from a libertarian perspective?

00:04:16.956 --> 00:04:18.958
- Well, he has cut
some regulations.

00:04:18.958 --> 00:04:22.328 align:start size:88% position:13%
However, I'd like to
point out that a tax cut

00:04:22.328 --> 00:04:26.699 align:start size:97% position:3%
is also going to be possibly
an increase in spending

00:04:26.699 --> 00:04:28.534 align:start size:94% position:6%
if they don't do
anything to make that up.

00:04:28.534 --> 00:04:29.602
So

00:04:29.602 --> 00:04:30.903
again,

00:04:30.903 --> 00:04:32.105
the bottom line...

00:04:32.105 --> 00:04:33.006
- Like the deficits are
going up either way.

00:04:33.006 --> 00:04:34.941
- Yeah, exactly.

00:04:34.941 --> 00:04:37.243
The bottom line is
spending's going up

00:04:37.243 --> 00:04:38.478
and that's what counts.

00:04:38.478 --> 00:04:40.113 align:start size:88% position:13%
Even if we're not
paying for it this year

00:04:40.113 --> 00:04:41.414
we would be paying
for it next year,

00:04:41.414 --> 00:04:43.116
10 years from now,
20 years from now

00:04:43.116 --> 00:04:44.817
and that's what matters.

00:04:45.952 --> 00:04:48.221
- Are you constantly
amazed as a libertarian

00:04:48.221 --> 00:04:53.192 align:start size:97% position:3%
that telling people we want
you to keep more of your money

00:04:53.192 --> 00:04:55.528
is not more of a winning ticket.

00:04:55.528 --> 00:04:57.630
I mean, I think when
people really hear it,

00:04:57.630 --> 00:04:59.265 align:start size:84% position:16%
if you bash them
over the head with it

00:04:59.265 --> 00:05:00.867
over and over and over
again and you're like,

00:05:00.867 --> 00:05:04.404 align:start size:94% position:6%
yeah, we want you to have
your money, not them.

00:05:04.404 --> 00:05:05.605
I think they do get it,

00:05:05.605 --> 00:05:07.473 align:start size:84% position:16%
but it seems like
it's such an easy sale

00:05:07.473 --> 00:05:10.176 align:start size:97% position:3%
and yet for some reason people
just don't understand it

00:05:10.176 --> 00:05:11.644
or don't absorb it.

00:05:12.812 --> 00:05:14.414 align:start size:84% position:16%
- Yes, well, what
really frustrates me

00:05:14.414 --> 00:05:17.183
are people like Bill Gates
or Oprah Winfrey who say,

00:05:17.183 --> 00:05:19.485 align:start size:97% position:3%
yeah, the government doesn't
take enough of my money.

00:05:19.485 --> 00:05:20.920
You know, text me more.

00:05:20.920 --> 00:05:22.822
But look at what
Bill Gates does.

00:05:22.822 --> 00:05:25.725 align:start size:94% position:6%
He starts the bill of
Melinda Gates Foundation,

00:05:25.725 --> 00:05:27.760
does, you know, good work

00:05:27.760 --> 00:05:30.630 align:start size:88% position:13%
and Oprah Winfrey
opens up her own school

00:05:30.630 --> 00:05:31.964
right over in Africa.

00:05:31.964 --> 00:05:34.067
Well, if they think
that the government

00:05:34.067 --> 00:05:36.402 align:start size:81% position:19%
can do a better
job than they can,

00:05:36.402 --> 00:05:38.504
why are they starting
their own foundations?

00:05:38.504 --> 00:05:40.707
Why not simply turn
all of that money

00:05:40.707 --> 00:05:42.175
over to the federal government?

00:05:42.175 --> 00:05:44.844 line:0%
And so I think that actions
speak louder than words.

00:05:44.844 --> 00:05:47.880 line:0%
And if even they aren't
turning their money over,

00:05:47.880 --> 00:05:49.549 line:0%
I think that that
just sent a message

00:05:49.549 --> 00:05:50.783
to everybody else that,

00:05:50.783 --> 00:05:52.385 align:start size:84% position:16%
Hey, the government
doesn't do a good job.

00:05:52.385 --> 00:05:55.421
I can't think of much that the
government does a better job

00:05:55.421 --> 00:05:56.723
than the private sector.

00:05:56.723 --> 00:05:59.359
And I think that bill
Gates and Oprah Winfrey

00:05:59.359 --> 00:06:02.528
and all these other liberals
who want bigger government,

00:06:02.528 --> 00:06:05.465
I think that they're just
proving our point for us.

00:06:05.465 --> 00:06:07.533 align:start size:97% position:3%
- So what do you think is
going on in their heads there?

00:06:07.533 --> 00:06:09.102
Is it just,

00:06:09.102 --> 00:06:12.338 align:start size:84% position:16%
is it misguidedness
or is it guilt

00:06:12.338 --> 00:06:16.175 align:start size:97% position:3%
or is it that they know that
the machine and the media

00:06:16.175 --> 00:06:19.545 align:start size:94% position:6%
will like them more if
they take these positions?

00:06:20.480 --> 00:06:22.582
- I'm hoping it's ignorance.

00:06:22.582 --> 00:06:24.484
The true sense of
the word ignorance.

00:06:24.484 --> 00:06:26.819
Because a lot of people
just don't understand

00:06:26.819 --> 00:06:28.054
how things work.

00:06:28.054 --> 00:06:29.522
And that's one of the
biggest compliments

00:06:29.522 --> 00:06:31.124
that I get from people

00:06:31.124 --> 00:06:32.625
just, you know, non
libertarian friends

00:06:32.625 --> 00:06:34.460 align:start size:88% position:13%
after they meet me,
they say, you know what?

00:06:34.460 --> 00:06:36.229
I read the news differently now,

00:06:36.229 --> 00:06:38.030
I look at things differently.

00:06:38.030 --> 00:06:40.233 align:start size:97% position:3%
They don't, you know, for
instance, yeah, we cut taxes.

00:06:40.233 --> 00:06:42.034
Okay, what about spending?

00:06:42.034 --> 00:06:44.504 align:start size:94% position:6%
So you can look at things
in a superficial way

00:06:44.504 --> 00:06:46.439
and think things are
going great without

00:06:46.439 --> 00:06:48.307
you know, the understanding

00:06:48.307 --> 00:06:51.911
or the underlying what's
going on beneath it all.

00:06:51.911 --> 00:06:56.215 align:start size:97% position:3%
- Yeah, does the thing that
frustrates you the most

00:06:56.215 --> 00:06:59.318
have anything to do with
the sort of simplistic way

00:06:59.318 --> 00:07:01.087
we look at politics
where, you know,

00:07:01.087 --> 00:07:03.089 align:start size:84% position:16%
half of the country
seems to think

00:07:03.089 --> 00:07:05.224
that if you tell them they're
getting something for free,

00:07:05.224 --> 00:07:07.727
they seem to think
it actually is free.

00:07:07.727 --> 00:07:11.130 align:start size:94% position:6%
And combating that notion
is almost impossible.

00:07:11.130 --> 00:07:13.933
You say free healthcare,
you say free education

00:07:13.933 --> 00:07:16.436 align:start size:94% position:6%
you know, free money now,
literally free money.

00:07:16.436 --> 00:07:20.773
It's like that combating, oh,
but you do have to pay for it.

00:07:20.773 --> 00:07:23.409
That's just not what we
do publicly very well.

00:07:24.844 --> 00:07:27.013
- Yes, I would have thought
that with the Obama phone,

00:07:27.013 --> 00:07:28.014
remember those?

00:07:29.415 --> 00:07:31.851 align:start size:97% position:3%
Basically what Obama was gonna
reach into his back pocket

00:07:31.851 --> 00:07:33.085
and buy everybody a phone.

00:07:33.085 --> 00:07:34.821
And that's what I've
been telling everybody

00:07:34.821 --> 00:07:37.256 align:start size:94% position:6%
about these $1,200 checks
that they're getting,

00:07:37.256 --> 00:07:39.892 align:start size:84% position:16%
is that money is
coming from somewhere.

00:07:39.892 --> 00:07:43.296 align:start size:97% position:3%
And I know that, you know,
supposedly there was a hold up

00:07:43.296 --> 00:07:44.964 align:start size:84% position:16%
because Donald Trump
wanted his name

00:07:44.964 --> 00:07:46.866
written on the actual check.

00:07:46.866 --> 00:07:49.168 align:start size:84% position:16%
Well, I don't think
that that check

00:07:49.168 --> 00:07:50.670
is coming from his back pocket

00:07:50.670 --> 00:07:52.205
or his private checking account,

00:07:52.205 --> 00:07:53.606
it's coming from us.

00:07:53.606 --> 00:07:55.475
So somehow they give us money

00:07:55.475 --> 00:07:57.310
and make it, you know,

00:07:57.310 --> 00:08:00.446
make it seem like it's a
Santa Claus or something.

00:08:00.446 --> 00:08:02.215
But what's frustrating is

00:08:03.516 --> 00:08:07.053 align:start size:88% position:13%
that they take our taxes
out, our income taxes

00:08:07.053 --> 00:08:11.958 align:start size:97% position:3%
so that we get a tax refund
every year after April.

00:08:11.958 --> 00:08:14.560
And so it looks like
we're getting something

00:08:14.560 --> 00:08:17.163
and I wish they had never
started that practice.

00:08:17.163 --> 00:08:19.098
I don't think we'd
be where we are now

00:08:19.098 --> 00:08:22.034
if people actually
had to feel the pain.

00:08:22.034 --> 00:08:24.070 align:start size:84% position:16%
And right now
people feel the pain

00:08:24.070 --> 00:08:26.239
when they're teenagers and
then they quickly forget.

00:08:26.239 --> 00:08:28.541
You know, so many times
I hear about somebody,

00:08:28.541 --> 00:08:31.444
you know, a friend's
kid who goes to work

00:08:31.444 --> 00:08:34.013
and like wait a minute, I
worked 20 hours this week.

00:08:34.013 --> 00:08:35.715
Where's this money going?

00:08:35.715 --> 00:08:38.184
And it's like, well, welcome
to the world of being an adult,

00:08:38.184 --> 00:08:39.652
welcome to the world of taxes.

00:08:39.652 --> 00:08:41.654
And so it feels painful then

00:08:41.654 --> 00:08:43.489 align:start size:84% position:16%
but by the time you're
30, 40 years old

00:08:43.489 --> 00:08:44.724
and it's grown and grown,

00:08:44.724 --> 00:08:47.326 align:start size:88% position:13%
you've kind of
forgotten about it, so.

00:08:47.326 --> 00:08:49.228
- Yeah, so I can't talk

00:08:49.228 --> 00:08:50.997 align:start size:84% position:16%
to the libertarian
presidential candidate

00:08:50.997 --> 00:08:53.766
without mentioning the
phrase that everyone says

00:08:53.766 --> 00:08:56.135 align:start size:94% position:6%
that getting libertarians
agree on anything

00:08:56.135 --> 00:08:57.837
is like hurting a bunch of cats.

00:08:57.837 --> 00:09:01.240 align:start size:88% position:13%
And I think when people
think of the party,

00:09:01.240 --> 00:09:02.475
the party itself,

00:09:02.475 --> 00:09:05.077
they think of the naked
guy running on stage,

00:09:05.077 --> 00:09:08.347 align:start size:88% position:13%
all the crazy characters
and everything else.

00:09:08.347 --> 00:09:13.352 align:start size:84% position:16%
What do you think
the libertarians have
perhaps done wrong

00:09:14.086 --> 00:09:15.721
if the ideas are right?

00:09:17.890 --> 00:09:22.061
- Well, I think what we
all did wrong decades ago

00:09:22.061 --> 00:09:25.164
was try to focus on philosophy.

00:09:25.164 --> 00:09:27.266 align:start size:84% position:16%
Although I think the
libertarian party

00:09:27.266 --> 00:09:28.768
pretty much had to do it

00:09:28.768 --> 00:09:33.372
because when the party started
40 years ago we didn't have,

00:09:33.372 --> 00:09:35.608
well, actually more than
40 years ago, 50 years ago,

00:09:35.608 --> 00:09:39.345
we didn't have all
of these outlets.

00:09:39.345 --> 00:09:41.347 align:start size:88% position:13%
We didn't have all
these educational groups

00:09:41.347 --> 00:09:43.082 align:start size:84% position:16%
all of these research
institutions.

00:09:43.082 --> 00:09:44.784
So we pretty much
had to do it all.

00:09:44.784 --> 00:09:46.385
So we focused on philosophy.

00:09:46.385 --> 00:09:47.920
And in fact,

00:09:47.920 --> 00:09:51.023
it's interesting reading the
original libertarian papers

00:09:51.023 --> 00:09:53.426 align:start size:97% position:3%
that talk about how we
shouldn't even run candidates.

00:09:53.426 --> 00:09:54.927
You know we're a political party

00:09:54.927 --> 00:09:57.630
and maybe not run candidates
because our job is to educate.

00:09:57.630 --> 00:09:59.932 align:start size:84% position:16%
Well now we no longer
need to do that.

00:09:59.932 --> 00:10:02.501
And so that's why I'm so
happy to be the candidate

00:10:02.501 --> 00:10:05.404
and I'm really glad that I
was able to draw together,

00:10:05.404 --> 00:10:09.609
both the pragmatic caucus
and the radical caucus

00:10:09.609 --> 00:10:13.012
who somewhat agreed on me,
because what I'm trying to do

00:10:13.012 --> 00:10:15.748
is I'm trying to give
a practical message

00:10:15.748 --> 00:10:17.249
to the American public

00:10:17.249 --> 00:10:19.085 align:start size:81% position:19%
and not talk about
cell ownership,

00:10:19.085 --> 00:10:22.421
not talk about me but talk
about, okay, you know what?

00:10:22.421 --> 00:10:24.156 align:start size:94% position:6%
You're having a hard
time paying your mortgage

00:10:24.156 --> 00:10:27.159 align:start size:88% position:13%
because your healthcare
bills are so high

00:10:27.159 --> 00:10:31.063 align:start size:94% position:6%
you know, or we hear about
people being sent off

00:10:31.063 --> 00:10:32.632
around the world and you know,

00:10:32.632 --> 00:10:34.367 align:start size:88% position:13%
your friends, your
neighbors your relatives

00:10:34.367 --> 00:10:36.435
being killed in a senseless war.

00:10:36.435 --> 00:10:39.672 align:start size:94% position:6%
So let's talk about things
that they care about

00:10:39.672 --> 00:10:41.273
and take off our philosophy hat

00:10:41.273 --> 00:10:43.576
and put on our political hat.

00:10:43.576 --> 00:10:46.712
- Yeah, do you think that
there's a better chance

00:10:46.712 --> 00:10:49.115
because of what you said earlier

00:10:49.115 --> 00:10:52.618 align:start size:84% position:16%
that this is the year
to make the dent?

00:10:52.618 --> 00:10:55.054
Because it seems to
me like there was,

00:10:55.054 --> 00:10:57.523 align:start size:84% position:16%
in the summer
before the election,

00:10:57.523 --> 00:11:00.793 align:start size:97% position:3%
there was suddenly this buzz
for a few weeks of like,

00:11:00.793 --> 00:11:04.463 align:start size:84% position:16%
Oh maybe there's this
libertarian thing
that could happen.

00:11:04.463 --> 00:11:07.767
Or at least, I mean, I
did a video in August

00:11:07.767 --> 00:11:09.201 align:start size:94% position:6%
when I said that I'm gonna
vote for Gary Johnson

00:11:09.201 --> 00:11:11.704 align:start size:88% position:13%
and I said, really
look, maybe he can't win

00:11:11.704 --> 00:11:15.141 align:start size:88% position:13%
but I at least wanna
get the guy in a debate.

00:11:15.141 --> 00:11:17.710 align:start size:84% position:16%
Now you did not
get in the debates.

00:11:17.710 --> 00:11:20.312
So I'm guessing you're
not too happy about that.

00:11:20.312 --> 00:11:23.115 align:start size:84% position:16%
But what about
combating the system?

00:11:23.115 --> 00:11:24.917
Like, can you just talk
about what it's been like

00:11:24.917 --> 00:11:27.486
to just combat the
two party thing?

00:11:28.988 --> 00:11:30.923
- Oh, it's been
an uphill battle.

00:11:30.923 --> 00:11:33.125
And what people
don't realize is,

00:11:33.125 --> 00:11:35.528 align:start size:81% position:19%
well, one thing
that I hate is how

00:11:35.528 --> 00:11:37.229
the libertarian party is put

00:11:37.229 --> 00:11:39.265
as one of the other
third parties, right?

00:11:39.265 --> 00:11:40.533
And I've been asked,

00:11:40.533 --> 00:11:42.368
will you debate the
other third parties?

00:11:42.368 --> 00:11:43.636
And my answer is no,

00:11:43.636 --> 00:11:45.204
because we need to be
on the debate stage

00:11:45.204 --> 00:11:47.073
with the democrats
and republicans.

00:11:47.073 --> 00:11:49.275
We are the only political party

00:11:49.275 --> 00:11:51.577 align:start size:88% position:13%
other than the Democrats
and Republicans

00:11:51.577 --> 00:11:54.880 align:start size:84% position:16%
to have a presidential
on the ballot

00:11:54.880 --> 00:11:56.982 align:start size:88% position:13%
and back to back
presidential elections.

00:11:56.982 --> 00:11:59.985 align:start size:84% position:16%
You know, we have
joined the adult table

00:11:59.985 --> 00:12:01.687
and that's the way we
need to be treated.

00:12:01.687 --> 00:12:04.223 align:start size:84% position:16%
And it is frustrating
but of course

00:12:04.223 --> 00:12:05.858
the Democrats and Republicans

00:12:05.858 --> 00:12:07.393
they don't want us anywhere near

00:12:07.393 --> 00:12:09.161
because we're going to show

00:12:09.161 --> 00:12:10.863
that there is a
real alternative.

00:12:10.863 --> 00:12:13.332
And we keep hearing
the media talk about,

00:12:14.967 --> 00:12:17.803 align:start size:94% position:6%
talk about, you know,
two old, rich white guys.

00:12:17.803 --> 00:12:20.239
And I would say, that's
not even the worst part.

00:12:20.239 --> 00:12:21.707
The worst part is,

00:12:21.707 --> 00:12:24.443
neither of whom is going to let
you make your own decisions.

00:12:24.443 --> 00:12:27.146
Neither of whom is going to
let you spend your own money.

00:12:27.146 --> 00:12:29.148
Neither of whom is going
to bring the troops home

00:12:29.148 --> 00:12:31.317
and neither of whom is
going to do anything

00:12:31.317 --> 00:12:32.918
about pushing healthcare costs.

00:12:32.918 --> 00:12:35.287 align:start size:88% position:13%
And so I've been telling
people #fakedebates

00:12:36.589 --> 00:12:39.492
because if we don't get
the message out there

00:12:39.492 --> 00:12:42.294
then people aren't going
to see a real alternative.

00:12:42.294 --> 00:12:44.263
Because there's really
not a big alternative.

00:12:44.263 --> 00:12:46.665
You know, they create
a lot of fake drama

00:12:46.665 --> 00:12:50.002
but they're both big government
people as we saw with Trump.

00:12:50.002 --> 00:12:52.638
And so now we'll just have
to wait and see what happens.

00:12:52.638 --> 00:12:55.508 align:start size:94% position:6%
And we hear the, you know,
the debate commission

00:12:55.508 --> 00:12:59.678 align:start position:0%
who of course is made up of
half democrats, half republicans

00:12:59.678 --> 00:13:01.881
you know, oh, it wouldn't
serve the American people.

00:13:01.881 --> 00:13:03.716 align:start size:81% position:19%
You know, too many
people on stage

00:13:03.716 --> 00:13:05.651
forgetting that, you
know, we saw what?

00:13:05.651 --> 00:13:08.120
Nine Democrats on
the stage at a time

00:13:08.120 --> 00:13:10.556
and they can't have
three or even four.

00:13:10.556 --> 00:13:13.626 align:start size:84% position:16%
And also when you
look at the debates,

00:13:13.626 --> 00:13:14.894
limiting it to two,

00:13:14.894 --> 00:13:17.062
it's not there to help
the American people.

00:13:17.062 --> 00:13:19.632 align:start size:97% position:3%
It's there to help the
democrat and republican party.

00:13:19.632 --> 00:13:22.401
They truly do have
a monopoly on that.

00:13:22.401 --> 00:13:24.069
- All right, so let's
back up for a second,

00:13:24.069 --> 00:13:25.604 align:start size:84% position:16%
because you mentioned
that 50 years ago

00:13:25.604 --> 00:13:27.072
there was this debate

00:13:27.072 --> 00:13:28.941 align:start size:97% position:3%
whether the libertarians were
even to run at candidate.

00:13:28.941 --> 00:13:32.278 align:start size:97% position:3%
So for some people that
are watching this right now

00:13:32.278 --> 00:13:35.214
that don't fully get
what a libertarian is

00:13:35.214 --> 00:13:38.918 align:start size:84% position:16%
can you do libertarian
101 and sort of

00:13:38.918 --> 00:13:40.452
what is,

00:13:40.452 --> 00:13:43.823 align:start size:97% position:3%
you know, the reason that it's
so hard to herd these cats

00:13:43.823 --> 00:13:45.324
is when you talk to libertarians

00:13:45.324 --> 00:13:47.026 align:start size:97% position:3%
there's always someone
that wants less government.

00:13:47.026 --> 00:13:48.994
So you get it to less and
then someone says less

00:13:48.994 --> 00:13:50.796
and then someone says
less and less and less

00:13:50.796 --> 00:13:53.232 align:start size:88% position:13%
until you're endlessly,
you know, everyone,

00:13:53.232 --> 00:13:55.868 align:start size:97% position:3%
it always ends in the debate
about driver's licenses

00:13:55.868 --> 00:13:57.136
or something like that.

00:13:57.136 --> 00:13:59.471
What is a libertarian to you?

00:14:00.840 --> 00:14:03.375 align:start size:97% position:3%
- I say libertarian is
somebody who's on your side

00:14:03.375 --> 00:14:05.845
and not the side
of the politicians,

00:14:05.845 --> 00:14:08.581 align:start size:97% position:3%
the bureaucrats, the lobbyists
and the special interests.

00:14:08.581 --> 00:14:12.117 align:start size:97% position:3%
And I tell people that, you
know, best what's best for you

00:14:12.117 --> 00:14:14.653 align:start size:97% position:3%
and not the people in
Washington pure and simple.

00:14:14.653 --> 00:14:17.756 align:start position:0%
You should be able to make
your decisions about education,

00:14:17.756 --> 00:14:18.624
healthcare,

00:14:19.725 --> 00:14:21.227
retirement,

00:14:21.227 --> 00:14:23.696
all of the things that are
going through the government

00:14:23.696 --> 00:14:27.066
you should be able to make
your own decision about.

00:14:27.066 --> 00:14:28.534
- Yeah, do you ever think that

00:14:28.534 --> 00:14:32.371 align:start position:0%
in a weird way, sort of I guess
in a depressing way somehow

00:14:32.371 --> 00:14:33.906
that the ship has sailed,

00:14:33.906 --> 00:14:36.675
that explaining to people why

00:14:36.675 --> 00:14:38.277
government shouldn't be involved

00:14:38.277 --> 00:14:40.512 align:start size:94% position:6%
or why you should keep
more of what you've earned

00:14:40.512 --> 00:14:42.514
or all of these things that

00:14:42.514 --> 00:14:43.782
it's sort of what we
talked about earlier,

00:14:43.782 --> 00:14:45.718
but intellectually they get it

00:14:45.718 --> 00:14:48.621
but it's sort of like they
can't even fathom a life

00:14:48.621 --> 00:14:52.324 align:start size:97% position:3%
where the government wouldn't
do all of these things.

00:14:52.324 --> 00:14:55.227
- Well, you know, I was
disheartened for awhile.

00:14:55.227 --> 00:14:58.697
However, with COVID
I'm seeing that,

00:14:58.697 --> 00:15:00.933
no, we haven't lost
our individualism.

00:15:00.933 --> 00:15:05.137
I was so ecstatic
to see those people

00:15:05.137 --> 00:15:07.573
storming around the
Michigan state house

00:15:07.573 --> 00:15:10.509 align:start size:97% position:3%
saying, hey, we're the land
of the free home of the brave,

00:15:10.509 --> 00:15:12.311
you can't lock us up like this.

00:15:12.311 --> 00:15:14.580
Or to see the Dallas hairdresser

00:15:14.580 --> 00:15:17.416
or to see what even
the shots we've seen

00:15:17.416 --> 00:15:19.318 align:start size:81% position:19%
of Nancy Pelosi
being a hypocrite.

00:15:19.318 --> 00:15:21.987
I think people are finally
saying, hey, wait a minute.

00:15:21.987 --> 00:15:24.189 align:start size:94% position:6%
This isn't what America's
supposed to be about.

00:15:24.189 --> 00:15:28.193 align:start position:0%
And so I think they're now
feeling, you know, libertarians

00:15:28.193 --> 00:15:30.963
you know, people like me who
joined the party decades ago

00:15:30.963 --> 00:15:34.433 align:start size:88% position:13%
we've always had this
yearning to have freedom

00:15:34.433 --> 00:15:36.635 align:start size:84% position:16%
and to have more
liberty in our lives.

00:15:36.635 --> 00:15:39.238 align:start size:97% position:3%
But I think the average person
probably didn't feel it.

00:15:39.238 --> 00:15:43.409 align:start position:0%
They didn't feel big government
upon them until recently.

00:15:43.409 --> 00:15:45.277
And they're being told
they have to wear a mask

00:15:45.277 --> 00:15:46.745
wherever they go

00:15:46.745 --> 00:15:48.447
and they're being told, nope,
you're under house arrest.

00:15:48.447 --> 00:15:50.549 align:start size:88% position:13%
You gotta stay home,
you can't go to your job

00:15:50.549 --> 00:15:54.353
and people I think are
beginning to question it.

00:15:54.353 --> 00:15:59.358
- Yeah, so what is the proper
libertarian response to COVID

00:16:00.526 --> 00:16:01.460
and lock downs and
everything else,

00:16:01.460 --> 00:16:02.661
if you were president, right?

00:16:02.661 --> 00:16:04.763
Or no, if you were
president in February

00:16:04.763 --> 00:16:06.899 align:start size:88% position:13%
and if you were
president or right now,

00:16:06.899 --> 00:16:09.068
what would be different?

00:16:09.068 --> 00:16:11.870 align:start size:88% position:13%
- Well, the biggest
mistake that Trump made

00:16:11.870 --> 00:16:14.873
was he didn't get the
FDA out of the way.

00:16:14.873 --> 00:16:18.177
And again, when people ask me
why I'm running for president

00:16:18.177 --> 00:16:19.778
is because government is too big

00:16:19.778 --> 00:16:22.014 align:start size:84% position:16%
too bossy, too
nosy, too intrusive.

00:16:22.014 --> 00:16:23.415
And the worst part is they hurt

00:16:23.415 --> 00:16:25.017 align:start size:88% position:13%
the very people
they're trying to help.

00:16:25.017 --> 00:16:28.053 align:start size:88% position:13%
The FDA is an excellent
example of that.

00:16:28.053 --> 00:16:31.790
That with the FDA, there
were dozens of testing kits

00:16:31.790 --> 00:16:34.760
that we could have had,
but the FDA blocked them.

00:16:34.760 --> 00:16:37.296 align:start size:97% position:3%
Originally, we were only
allowed to have two of them.

00:16:37.296 --> 00:16:40.299
So meanwhile Southeast Asia,
they're doing extensive testing

00:16:40.299 --> 00:16:43.235
seeing who needs to stay home
and who can go out and work.

00:16:43.235 --> 00:16:46.005 align:start size:94% position:6%
In the meantime, we're
shutting down our economy.

00:16:46.005 --> 00:16:47.473
And on top of that, we had

00:16:48.974 --> 00:16:51.543 align:start size:84% position:16%
Trump up on stage
with Dr. Fauci saying,

00:16:51.543 --> 00:16:53.178
you know what if you
don't have symptoms,

00:16:53.178 --> 00:16:54.780
no need to get tested.

00:16:54.780 --> 00:16:57.449
Well, at the very
time he said that

00:16:57.449 --> 00:16:59.351 align:start size:84% position:16%
they knew that over
half the people

00:16:59.351 --> 00:17:01.653
or at least that was
the wisdom at the time,

00:17:01.653 --> 00:17:02.888
that over half the people

00:17:02.888 --> 00:17:05.190
who had the virus had
no symptoms at all.

00:17:05.190 --> 00:17:07.359 align:start size:88% position:13%
So no that's the time
you need to have testing

00:17:07.359 --> 00:17:09.461 align:start size:84% position:16%
when you don't know
if you have it or not.

00:17:11.063 --> 00:17:13.198
- And what about the
lockdown specifically?

00:17:14.366 --> 00:17:15.467
- Yes, well,

00:17:16.335 --> 00:17:19.204
about the testing specifically

00:17:19.204 --> 00:17:22.074
that we basically, they
were locking us down

00:17:22.074 --> 00:17:25.077
because they didn't know
who would be healthy enough

00:17:25.077 --> 00:17:26.578
to be out on the streets.

00:17:26.578 --> 00:17:30.249
So how about testing us,
letting us test ourselves

00:17:30.249 --> 00:17:31.517
and then we would know.

00:17:31.517 --> 00:17:33.819 align:start size:84% position:16%
And here's the irony
from my part is

00:17:33.819 --> 00:17:36.255 align:start size:84% position:16%
one of my grandfathers
is from Sweden

00:17:36.255 --> 00:17:40.559 align:start size:94% position:6%
and his family immigrated
here to have freedom,

00:17:40.559 --> 00:17:42.594
to have the freedom that
they didn't have in Sweden.

00:17:42.594 --> 00:17:44.797
And yet Sweden's

00:17:44.797 --> 00:17:47.266
stores and shopping malls

00:17:47.266 --> 00:17:51.403 align:start size:88% position:13%
and restaurants and
schools all stayed open.

00:17:51.403 --> 00:17:54.006
So they're able to
move around freely.

00:17:54.006 --> 00:17:57.276 align:start size:88% position:13%
Meanwhile, we supposedly
the land of the free

00:17:57.276 --> 00:17:59.578 align:start size:84% position:16% line:0%
that people immigrate
to for freedom.

00:17:59.578 --> 00:18:00.813 line:0%
We're all under house arrest.

00:18:00.813 --> 00:18:02.381 line:0%
So that's just a travesty.

00:18:02.381 --> 00:18:04.616 line:0%
So it's just rather
ironic that my family

00:18:04.616 --> 00:18:06.085
came here for freedom

00:18:06.085 --> 00:18:08.053 align:start size:97% position:3%
and that the old country
was giving them more freedom

00:18:08.053 --> 00:18:10.122
at least in this regard.

00:18:10.122 --> 00:18:13.792
- Right, so would you
have left the decisions

00:18:13.792 --> 00:18:15.661
about lockdowns up to the States

00:18:15.661 --> 00:18:18.664 align:start size:97% position:3%
because in effect that's what
Trump basically has done.

00:18:18.664 --> 00:18:21.867
I assume that you're
okay with that, right?

00:18:21.867 --> 00:18:24.970 align:start size:97% position:3%
You wouldn't have wanted
this to be a federal mandate.

00:18:24.970 --> 00:18:27.406
- Well, again, actions
speak louder than words.

00:18:27.406 --> 00:18:30.876 align:start size:88% position:13%
Trump was encouraging
the States to lock down.

00:18:30.876 --> 00:18:33.278
I think the governors
were following his lead

00:18:33.278 --> 00:18:35.714
because the president is
in a role of leadership.

00:18:35.714 --> 00:18:38.517 align:start position:0%
And I think they were only
doing what he wanted them to do.

00:18:38.517 --> 00:18:40.052
So now he's saying open back up,

00:18:40.052 --> 00:18:42.688
yeah, but you already
told us to close down.

00:18:42.688 --> 00:18:46.925
So he shouldn't have given
that message to begin with.

00:18:46.925 --> 00:18:50.796
And what frustrates me
is it's one more example

00:18:50.796 --> 00:18:54.633
where people are thinking that
they only have one decision,

00:18:54.633 --> 00:18:57.336
that we should all vote
and have one decision.

00:18:57.336 --> 00:19:00.739 align:start size:97% position:3%
And you know, people are
under the mistaken impression

00:19:00.739 --> 00:19:03.208 align:start size:97% position:3%
that if the government
doesn't tell us to wear masks

00:19:03.208 --> 00:19:04.743
we're not going to wear masks.

00:19:04.743 --> 00:19:07.012
And Walmart shot that down.

00:19:07.012 --> 00:19:10.449 align:start size:94% position:6%
Walmart has a policy where
you have to wear a mask

00:19:10.449 --> 00:19:11.917
if you're, if you work there,

00:19:11.917 --> 00:19:14.453
if you're a vendor, if
you're a shopper, whoever

00:19:14.453 --> 00:19:16.221
you have to wear a
mask and Walmart.

00:19:16.221 --> 00:19:18.257
So why can't we have a world

00:19:18.257 --> 00:19:21.360 align:start size:97% position:3%
in which we vote with our
feet or vote with our dollars.

00:19:21.360 --> 00:19:24.763
If we wanna wear a mask,
then we go to Walmart.

00:19:24.763 --> 00:19:27.199
And if we don't want to wear
masks, we go to other stores.

00:19:27.199 --> 00:19:28.700
Why can't we have that?

00:19:28.700 --> 00:19:31.370 align:start size:97% position:3%
And it's really frustrating
because on my local news show,

00:19:32.604 --> 00:19:35.174
my mayor of the
city where I live

00:19:35.174 --> 00:19:37.409
required, started
requiring a mask

